# References and links: {number of: id} writes the number of a list item, a numbered heading or a figure.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: References and links · Number of a box
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Heading 2
			Typography:
				Numbered: true
		For element: Heading 3
			Typography:
				Numbered: true
		For element: List
			Box:
				Padding: 0 0 0 20
				Margin: 0 0 10 0
		For element: Figure
			Typography:
				Number label: Figure {number}.
			Box:
				Margin: 4 0 10 0
		For element: Caption
			Typography:
				Size: 8.5
				Color: muted
			Box:
				Margin: 4 0 0 0
	Section:
		Text: References and links
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Number of a box
		Paragraph: `{{number of: id}}` writes the number that the engine gives a box: the number of an item of a numbered list (`b`), the complete number of a numbered heading (`1.2`) or the number of a figure (`1`), without its label.
			Style: intro
		Text: Paragraph: ... clause {{number of: payment}} ... section {{number of: install}} ... figure {{number of: emblem}}.
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Payment follows clause {number of: payment}, the steps are in section {number of: install} and the emblem is in figure {number of: emblem}.
			Style: target
		Heading 2:
			Text: Terms
		List:
			Marker: lower-alpha
			Marker suffix: parenthesis
			List item:
				Paragraph: The goods travel at the risk of the buyer.
			List item:
				Id: payment
				Paragraph: Payment is made within 30 days. (Id: payment)
		Heading 3:
			Text: Delivery
		Paragraph: Delivery takes two weeks.
		Heading 3:
			Id: install
			Text: Installation (Id: install)
		Paragraph: The installation is done by the workshop.
		Figure:
			Id: emblem
			Caption: The emblem of the workshop (Id: emblem).
			Image: examples/menu/emblem.svg
				Alt: Emblem of the workshop
				Box:
					Width: 60
